   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Period Drop\n\nA word rises out of its line, then a colored dot falls from above the frame, bounces with squash and stretch, and settles as the period.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 2.5 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- An end card or a logo lockup should land with one physical, memorable beat.\n- A brand word should finish with a colored period, as in a wordmark.\n- A statement needs a full stop that the viewer actually sees arrive.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The lockup is a row of brand marks rather than a word: use logo-enter.\n- The word should only rise out of its line, with no accent: use mask-reveal-up.\n- The ending should be quiet, without any bounce: use soft-blur-in.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"studio\"\n- color (color): Text color, default \"#fafafa\"\n- dot_color (color): Dot color, default \"#ff4d1a\"\n- font_size (number, 60-280): Font size, default 160\n- font_weight (number, 100-900): Weight, default 800\n- dot_size (number, 0.08-0.5): Dot size, default 0.2\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Period Drop\n\n  A word rises out of its line, then a colored dot falls from above the frame, bounces with squash and stretch, and settles as the period.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/period-drop/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"period-drop\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"2.5\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Text\", \"description\": \"Word that rises, then gets its period.\", \"default\": \"studio\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Text color\", \"description\": \"Color of the word.\", \"default\": \"#fafafa\"},\n    {\"id\": \"dot_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Dot color\", \"description\": \"Color of the falling period.\", \"default\": \"#ff4d1a\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Text size in reference pixels (720 high stage); long words shrink to fit.\", \"default\": 160, \"min\": 60, \"max\": 280, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_weight\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Weight\", \"description\": \"Font weight, 100 to 900.\", \"default\": 800, \"min\": 100, \"max\": 900, \"step\": 100},\n    {\"id\": \"dot_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Dot size\", \"description\": \"Dot diameter in em.\", \"default\": 0.2, \"min\": 0.08, \"max\": 0.5, \"step\": 0.01, \"unit\": \"em\"},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed multiplier.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.05, \"unit\": \"x\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Period Drop</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@100..900&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .pd-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; overflow: hidden; font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; }\n        .pd-line { line-height: 1; white-space: pre; }\n        .pd-cell { display: inline-block; overflow: hidden; padding-bottom: 0.15em; margin-bottom: -0.15em; vertical-align: top; }\n        .pd-char { display: inline-block; }\n        .pd-dot { display: inline-block; margin-left: 0.04em; border-radius: 50%; transform-origin: 50% 100%; visibility: hidden; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"period-drop\" data-duration=\"2.5\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"pd-clip\" class=\"pd-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"2.5\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"pd-line\" class=\"pd-line\"></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/CustomEase.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, options, fallback) {\n              return options.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            function col(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              if (typeof value === \"boolean\") return value;\n              if (value === \"true\") return true;\n              if (value === \"false\") return false;\n              return fallback;\n            }\n            function fit(el, maxPx, size, ratio) {\n              // Shrink el's font size until its scrollWidth fits ratio of the frame width.\n              el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var max = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * (ratio || 0.9));\n              if (el.scrollWidth > max) { size = Math.max(10, size * (max / el.scrollWidth)); el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; }\n              return size;\n            }\n            gsap.registerPlugin(CustomEase);\n            function ease(name, a, b, c, d) { return CustomEase.create(name, \"M0,0 C\" + a + \",\" + b + \" \" + c + \",\" + d + \" 1,1\"); }\n            function mulberry32(a) { return function () { a |= 0; a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0; var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a); t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t; return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; }; }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"2.5\");\n            function ip(t, a, b, from, to, e) {\n              var p = b === a ? 1 : (t - a) / (b - a);\n              p = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, p));\n              if (e) p = e(p);\n              return from + (to - from) * p;\n            }\n            function hash01(seed) {\n              var h = 2166136261;\n              for (var i = 0; i < seed.length; i++) { h ^= seed.charCodeAt(i); h = Math.imul(h, 16777619); }\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 2246822519);\n              return ((h ^ (h >>> 16)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n            }\n            function hashRange(seed, lo, hi) { return lo + hash01(seed) * (hi - lo); }\n            // Snap a frame number down to a stop-motion pose.\n            function qf(frame, step) { return Math.floor(frame / step + 1e-6) * step; }\n            function kf(t, keys, vals, e) {\n              if (t <= keys[0]) return vals[0];\n              for (var i = 0; i < keys.length - 1; i++) if (t <= keys[i + 1]) return ip(t, keys[i], keys[i + 1], vals[i], vals[i + 1], e);\n              return vals[vals.length - 1];\n            }\n            // Per-frame drawing: a pure function of the timeline time, run from a tween's onUpdate.\n            function tick(draw) {\n              tl.to({}, { duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(tl.time()); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n            }\n            var cubOut = ease(\"cub-out\", 0.215, 0.61, 0.355, 1);\n            var cubIn = ease(\"cub-in\", 0.55, 0.055, 0.675, 0.19);\n            var cubInOut = ease(\"cub-io\", 0.645, 0.045, 0.355, 1);\n\n            var line = document.getElementById(\"pd-line\");\n            var text = str(vars.text, \"studio\"), speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.25, 4);\n            var weight = num(vars.font_weight, 800, 100, 900), dotSize = num(vars.dot_size, 0.2, 0.08, 0.5);\n            var unit = Math.min(root.clientWidth / 1280, root.clientHeight / 720);\n            line.style.color = col(vars.color, \"#fafafa\");\n            line.style.fontWeight = weight; line.style.fontVariationSettings = '\"wght\" ' + weight;\n            var chars = Array.from(text).map(function (ch) {\n              var cell = document.createElement(\"span\"); cell.className = \"pd-cell\";\n              var inner = document.createElement(\"span\"); inner.className = \"pd-char\"; inner.textContent = ch;\n              cell.appendChild(inner); line.appendChild(cell); return inner;\n            });\n            var dotEl = document.createElement(\"span\");\n            dotEl.className = \"pd-dot\"; dotEl.style.width = dotSize + \"em\"; dotEl.style.height = dotSize + \"em\";\n            dotEl.style.background = col(vars.dot_color, \"#ff4d1a\");\n            line.appendChild(dotEl);\n            fit(line, 0, num(vars.font_size, 160, 60, 280) * unit, 0.9);\n            var drop = 0.62 * root.clientHeight;\n            var DROP = 20, FALL = 12, REST = 0.35, BOUNCES = 2, STRETCH = 0.3, SQUASH = 0.22, RECOVER = 1.1;\n            var outQuart = function (p) { return 1 - Math.pow(1 - p, 4); };\n            var impacts = [DROP + FALL];\n            for (var n = 1; n <= BOUNCES; n++) impacts.push(impacts[n - 1] + 2 * Math.pow(REST, n) * FALL);\n            // Gravity comes from the fall: g = 2 / fall^2, so the landing speed is 2 / fall.\n            function dotAt(t) {\n              if (t < DROP) return { visible: false, y: -1, sx: 1, sy: 1 };\n              var g = 2 / (FALL * FALL), landing = g * FALL, y = 0, sp = 0, deform = 0;\n              if (t < impacts[0]) {\n                var u = t - DROP; y = -1 + 0.5 * g * u * u; sp = g * u; deform = sp / landing;\n              } else {\n                var k = impacts.length - 1;\n                while (k > 0 && t < impacts[k]) k--;\n                var tau = t - impacts[k], bounce = k + 1;\n                var launch = bounce < impacts.length ? Math.pow(REST, bounce) * landing : 0;\n                var flight = launch > 0 ? (2 * launch) / g : 0;\n                if (tau < flight) { y = -(launch * tau - 0.5 * g * tau * tau); sp = Math.abs(launch - g * tau); }\n                var decay = Math.exp(-tau / RECOVER);\n                deform = -Math.pow(REST, k) * decay + (1 - decay) * (sp / landing);\n              }\n              if (Math.abs(deform) < 0.005) deform = 0;\n              var sy = deform >= 0 ? 1 + STRETCH * deform : 1 + SQUASH * Math.max(-1, deform);\n              return { visible: true, y: Math.min(0, y), sx: 1 / sy, sy: sy };\n            }\n            tick(function (tt) {\n              var t = tt * 30 * speed;\n              chars.forEach(function (el, i) {\n                el.style.transform = \"translateY(\" + ip(t, 2 * i, 2 * i + 12, 1, 0, outQuart) * 115 + \"%)\";\n              });\n              var d = dotAt(t);\n              dotEl.style.visibility = d.visible ? \"visible\" : \"hidden\";\n              dotEl.style.transform = \"translateY(\" + d.y * drop + \"px) scale(\" + d.sx + \",\" + d.sy + \")\";\n            });\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"2.5\");\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"period-drop\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
